From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 22:54:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 344/638] gamepad: reuse the portable Linux mapping table on
 AROS

AROS supplies its own HID transport, but the standard controller mapping function is a pure data/translation layer. Compile that implementation without importing Linux udev or hid-writer sources.

AI_PHASE: chromium-shared-cef

AI_STATUS: exact-link-gap-fixed-under-validation

AI_VALIDATION: registered native link contained exactly one unresolved GetGamepadStandardMappingFunction symbol

AI_LIMITATIONS: controller runtime input and native CEF link remain pending

AI_EVIDENCE: aros-opal-hosted-clean/test-artifacts/-cef-zero-v8-native-link-20260725/04-undefined-symbols.txt

AI_DECISION_CHAIN:
---
 device/gamepad/BUILD.gn | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/device/gamepad/BUILD.gn b/device/gamepad/BUILD.gn
index 93b5bf78e1..d09b7c1251 100644
--- a/device/gamepad/BUILD.gn
+++ b/device/gamepad/BUILD.gn
@@ -115,6 +115,12 @@ component("gamepad") {
     }
   }
 
+  if (is_aros) {
+    # USB/HID transport is provided by AROS, but the controller mapping table
+    # is platform-neutral and shared with the Linux input conventions.
+    sources += [ "gamepad_standard_mappings_linux.cc" ]
+  }
+
   if (is_android) {
     sources += [
       "gamepad_platform_data_fetcher_android.cc",
